Stop Using UWorld Decrypt — Get World Through GEngine Instead
i recently got back into making cheats, and honestly, the stupidity I’ve seen is abysmal.

FOR THE LOVE OF GOD, STOP USING UWORLD DECRYPT. IT’S TERRIBLE.

There are a million other ways to get UWorld, and I’m going to go through one of them for you skids.

Instead of relying on a constantly changing encrypted UWorld pointer, you can retrieve it through the engine’s existing object chain:

Code:

     
    Module Base
        ↓
    GEngine
        ↓
    GameViewport
        ↓
    World

Here is a basic example:

Code:

    #include "../memory/ProcessMemory.h"
     
    #include <cstdint>
     
    namespace offsets
    {
        constexpr std::uintptr_t GEngine      = 0x19DE55F8;
        constexpr std::uintptr_t GameViewport = 0xB70;
        constexpr std::uintptr_t World        = 0x78;
    }
     
    std::uintptr_t GetWorldFromGEngine()
    {
        auto& memory = memory::ProcessMemory::instance();
     
        const std::uintptr_t moduleBase = memory.get_module_base();
        if (!moduleBase)
            return 0;
     
        const std::uintptr_t engine =
            memory.read<std::uintptr_t>(moduleBase + offsets::GEngine);
     
        if (!engine)
            return 0;
     
        const std::uintptr_t viewport =
            memory.read<std::uintptr_t>(engine + offsets::GameViewport);
     
        if (!viewport)
            return 0;
     
        return memory.read<std::uintptr_t>(viewport + offsets::World);
    }
     
    void ExampleUsage()
    {
        const std::uintptr_t world = GetWorldFromGEngine();
     
        if (!world)
            return;
     
        // Use world here.
    }
